WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:25.451
Support Admin Watch on
kissasia.cam or kisskh.org

00:00:35.223 --> 00:00:39.061
HEROES NEXT DOOR

00:00:42.105 --> 00:00:42.981
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION.
ALL CHARACTERS, PROFESSIONS, PLACES,

00:00:43.065 --> 00:00:44.107
COMPANIES, ORGANIZATIONS,
ETHNIC GROUPS AND EVENTS ARE NOT REAL.

00:00:44.191 --> 00:00:45.150
ALL CHILD AND ANIMAL SCENES WERE FILMED
SAFELY UNDER EXPERT SUPERVISION.

00:00:47.778 --> 00:00:50.614
MINISTER OF NATIONAL DEFENSE: KIM SEOK-JUN

00:00:50.697 --> 00:00:52.407
CYBER OPERATIONS COMMAND:
BRIGADIER GENERAL KIM DO-HYEONG, UNIT 900

00:00:52.491 --> 00:00:54.159
LOGISTIC SUPPORT GROUP COMMANDER:
COLONEL JANG JUN-HUI

00:00:56.244 --> 00:00:58.455
If it's a modified Composition C-4...

00:00:58.538 --> 00:00:59.665
DEFENSE ACQUISITION PROGRAM ADMINISTRATOR:
KANG JUNG-GI

00:00:59.748 --> 00:01:01.708
It's definitely the bomb
we snuck away then.

00:01:01.792 --> 00:01:04.711
I know, I'm looking at it right now!

00:01:04.961 --> 00:01:06.630
Why point out the obvious?

00:01:08.215 --> 00:01:10.300
Am I asking you if the bomb belongs to us?

00:01:10.425 --> 00:01:13.345
I'm asking what it's doing out there!

00:01:15.138 --> 00:01:17.265
Have you checked the inventory count?

00:01:18.225 --> 00:01:21.561
Yes, and the said bomb
isn't used in the military anymore.

00:01:22.062 --> 00:01:25.065
The ones used last time
were classified as mission supplies.

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:27.943
Exactly. We exported all of them abroad.

00:01:28.443 --> 00:01:31.697
So, how did an exported bomb
make a U-turn and return to Korea?

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:34.366
Maybe there was
an issue with the delivery.

00:01:34.449 --> 00:01:36.326
They paid us the right amount.

00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:38.328
That means they definitely got the goods.

00:01:38.412 --> 00:01:39.788
Could it be...

00:01:40.872 --> 00:01:42.999
an act of terrorism?

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:44.876
Had that been the case,

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:49.548
the terrorists would've come forward,
demanding something!

00:01:50.257 --> 00:01:52.843
And why would any terrorist organization
want to target Kiyun-si?

00:01:52.926 --> 00:01:54.052
It's not even Seoul!

00:01:54.136 --> 00:01:55.929
You're so thick-headed.

00:01:58.390 --> 00:01:59.349
Listen up.

00:01:59.933 --> 00:02:02.436
Whatever it is,

00:02:02.894 --> 00:02:06.606
make sure the guys
who were at the site stay quiet.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:07.941
Keep a good eye on them.

00:02:08.108 --> 00:02:12.404
If this goes wrong,
it's over for all of us. Got it?

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:26.209
- Yes, sir.
- Tell all the ones on leave to return.

00:02:26.293 --> 00:02:27.335
Yes, sir.

00:02:27.753 --> 00:02:31.715
Cyber Operations Command,
Logistics Support Group,

00:02:32.424 --> 00:02:34.134
and the Defense Acquisition Program
Administrator?

00:02:36.428 --> 00:02:37.929
What were they doing together?

00:02:48.064 --> 00:02:52.986
MY BESTIE'S BESTIE IS MY BESTIE TOO

00:02:55.155 --> 00:02:57.240
YOU'RE MAKING THINGS COMPLICATED
JDD SPECIAL OPERATIONS FORCES, CHOI KANG

00:03:02.037 --> 00:03:03.121
They know me?

00:03:04.873 --> 00:03:06.792
Does this unit actually exist?

00:03:06.875 --> 00:03:09.544
Are you really from the JDD unit?

00:03:10.295 --> 00:03:13.048
I've never heard
of the JDD Special Operations Forces.

00:03:13.131 --> 00:03:16.426
- You know the Jindo Dog Alert? So--
- Wait.

00:03:16.802 --> 00:03:18.178
- Look at this.
- At what?

00:03:18.261 --> 00:03:19.387
Look at this.

00:03:23.725 --> 00:03:24.851
"A new day is...

00:03:27.729 --> 00:03:28.855
coming"?

00:03:31.107 --> 00:03:31.983
A NEW DAY IS COMING

00:03:33.026 --> 00:03:34.236
It shut down.

00:03:34.319 --> 00:03:36.238
What's going on? What happened?

00:03:37.989 --> 00:03:39.616
It's completely shut down.

00:03:43.703 --> 00:03:46.414
Why? Did you break it?

00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:50.168
So, what now?

00:03:51.044 --> 00:03:53.129
"A new day is coming"?

00:03:53.797 --> 00:03:55.674
What does that mean?

00:04:00.595 --> 00:04:03.723
How should I know?
I'm just reading what's on the screen.

00:04:04.599 --> 00:04:06.184
I can read, too, you know?

00:04:06.518 --> 00:04:07.894
What I want to ask is--

00:04:07.978 --> 00:04:11.273
Mr. Choi, get changed first.

00:04:11.565 --> 00:04:13.066
Thank you.

00:04:13.275 --> 00:04:14.985
Are you sure you're fine?

00:04:15.068 --> 00:04:17.320
Are you sure you're not hurt badly
under your shirt?

00:04:18.655 --> 00:04:20.407
I'm fine.

00:04:24.327 --> 00:04:26.162
I told you not to follow me.

00:04:26.246 --> 00:04:30.542
I mean, we also need to see
what happened...

00:04:33.461 --> 00:04:34.546
What?

00:04:38.133 --> 00:04:39.551
He definitely died.

00:04:40.051 --> 00:04:41.219
They cleaned it up so quickly.

00:04:42.053 --> 00:04:43.680
Do they have a cleanup crew with them?

00:04:46.057 --> 00:04:48.935
What is this? I don't see anyone.

00:04:49.644 --> 00:04:51.938
Are you sure you fought someone here?

00:04:52.022 --> 00:04:55.734
Are you sure
that's not chili powder and ketchup?

00:04:56.526 --> 00:04:59.446
Try tasting it, then.

00:04:59.613 --> 00:05:01.239
You think I'm that bored?

00:05:01.698 --> 00:05:02.908
My gosh!

00:05:03.575 --> 00:05:04.534
- What?
- What?

00:05:06.286 --> 00:05:07.579
It's so clean.

00:05:07.954 --> 00:05:10.707
I've never seen these urinals this clean!

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:11.666
Man!

00:05:12.125 --> 00:05:13.293
You're right.

00:05:14.002 --> 00:05:14.961
Damn.

00:05:15.337 --> 00:05:16.963
Are you kidding me?

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:20.258
How do we check the security cameras
in the hallway and the exit?

00:05:20.383 --> 00:05:22.677
The management office.

00:05:25.388 --> 00:05:29.643
That's odd. Is the memory full?
Why did it not record anything only here?

00:05:29.726 --> 00:05:32.854
Someone seems to have tampered with it.

00:05:34.147 --> 00:05:35.607
They would've gotten rid of it all.

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:37.859
That quickly?

00:05:38.318 --> 00:05:41.488
You're saying they cleaned the bathroom
and took care of the security cameras too?

00:05:41.905 --> 00:05:43.198
These guys are pros.

00:05:43.281 --> 00:05:45.158
They seem to have
a cleanup crew with them.

00:05:45.241 --> 00:05:48.411
A cleanup crew?
To clean up after all the mess?

00:05:49.955 --> 00:05:52.248
I should've just walked away
when he mentioned North Korean spies.

00:05:52.707 --> 00:05:55.168
Let's report it to the police first.

00:05:55.460 --> 00:05:56.670
What will we tell them?

00:05:56.753 --> 00:05:58.880
That you beat someone up
on your way to take a dump?

00:05:59.047 --> 00:06:02.300
We need to leave a record of it
in case we get blamed later.

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:03.635
Good point.

00:06:03.718 --> 00:06:05.845
Hey, contact Officer Park.

00:06:05.929 --> 00:06:08.556
No, call the police hotline.

00:06:08.932 --> 00:06:10.809
An informal report to an officer won't do.

00:06:10.892 --> 00:06:12.811
Okay, but what should we say?

00:06:12.894 --> 00:06:14.562
That you went to take a dump
and beat someone up?

00:06:14.646 --> 00:06:17.065
Hey. Don't mention the dump.

00:06:17.148 --> 00:06:19.442
What if they ask
why he went to the bathroom?

00:06:30.829 --> 00:06:34.040
Tell me more about the JDD unit.
Is it real?

00:06:34.124 --> 00:06:36.501
- Is there really such a unit in Korea?
- Exactly.

00:06:36.668 --> 00:06:37.961
No comment.

00:06:38.211 --> 00:06:39.546
Oh, you can't tell us?

00:06:40.797 --> 00:06:42.257
That means it's real.

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:45.093
JDD? Is it short for "Jindo dog"?

00:06:45.176 --> 00:06:46.845
No comment.

00:06:47.095 --> 00:06:49.097
I heard you're only deployed
on high-risk combat missions.

00:06:50.265 --> 00:06:52.100
Not even other military units know of it.

00:06:53.226 --> 00:06:54.811
And it doesn't belong
to the Ministry of National Defense.

00:06:54.894 --> 00:06:56.104
Are these all true?

00:06:56.187 --> 00:06:57.564
That's incredible.

00:07:02.736 --> 00:07:05.321
Where did you hear all that?

00:07:05.405 --> 00:07:08.116
Who discusses state secrets so openly?

00:07:09.659 --> 00:07:13.329
No comment, okay? Stop asking me about it.

00:07:13.413 --> 00:07:14.706
Yes, sir.

00:07:15.707 --> 00:07:17.417
Sure, whatever.

00:07:20.045 --> 00:07:22.047
Right. What are you going to do with that?

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:24.632
- What's your plan?
- Oh, this?

00:07:24.966 --> 00:07:28.845
I thought about reporting it to the cops,
but I missed my time to do it.

00:07:29.512 --> 00:07:31.848
We can give it to them,
but let's check the files in it first.

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:35.602
And please get me a copy of the footage
of the accident at the intersection.

00:07:35.685 --> 00:07:37.604
Great idea. You can do it, right?

00:07:37.687 --> 00:07:41.441
They used a remote control
to factory reset the settings.

00:07:42.358 --> 00:07:44.486
But I'll try it.
I'll set up the equipment today.

00:07:45.487 --> 00:07:46.738
Okay, goodnight, then.

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:48.281
Okay.

00:07:48.364 --> 00:07:51.659
- Goodnight, Mr. Choi!
- Goodnight.

00:07:55.872 --> 00:07:59.626
Man... He really is from JDD.

00:08:00.085 --> 00:08:04.547
Everything makes sense now,
with the gun and all.

00:08:04.631 --> 00:08:06.841
So, he's the Jason Bourne of Korea.
Amazing.

00:08:07.133 --> 00:08:11.262
He's much scarier than we thought.

00:08:11.387 --> 00:08:13.389
Look at how they recognized him
immediately.

00:08:13.973 --> 00:08:17.435
Choi Kang, look at what you've done to us.

00:08:18.561 --> 00:08:19.771
- Byeong-nam.
- Yeah?

00:08:19.854 --> 00:08:23.775
Isn't it better for us
that we have him on our side?

00:08:24.109 --> 00:08:26.653
What is this? A soccer match? What side?

00:08:28.029 --> 00:08:30.073
But he's definitely not
on the other side, right?

00:08:30.156 --> 00:08:33.701
Of course not!
Enough with the pointless doubts!

00:08:35.453 --> 00:08:39.833
Hey, you're always on the computer,
hacking or whatever,

00:08:39.916 --> 00:08:42.585
but you were so useless earlier.

00:08:43.419 --> 00:08:46.297
I wouldn't have expected
any more from you.

00:08:47.423 --> 00:08:48.967
They suddenly started
remote-controlling it,

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:50.301
and I've never seen this laptop model!

00:08:50.385 --> 00:08:51.719
- Sure.
- I was just confused, okay?

00:08:51.803 --> 00:08:53.847
Sure, you were.

00:08:54.264 --> 00:08:55.557
- Hey.
- What?

00:08:56.266 --> 00:08:59.477
I'll look into it, but you can take it.

00:08:59.769 --> 00:09:02.188
I can't put the kids at my gym at risk.

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:04.315
You can't put the kids at risk,
but I'm okay?

00:09:05.817 --> 00:09:06.943
Give it.

00:09:09.696 --> 00:09:11.948
- And Byeong-nam.
- What now?

00:09:12.031 --> 00:09:15.785
Invite Mr. Choi
to the hardware store from now on.

00:09:17.203 --> 00:09:19.372
Man, where are your balls?

00:09:19.455 --> 00:09:21.457
Seriously.

00:09:22.584 --> 00:09:25.003
Fine. Go now.

00:09:25.378 --> 00:09:26.796
I'm also walking that way.

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:28.298
Oh, right. Come.

00:09:38.933 --> 00:09:41.102
SPECIAL MARTIAL ARTS

00:09:52.030 --> 00:09:54.365
Honey, what are you doing there?

00:09:55.366 --> 00:09:56.910
I was just going to the bathroom.

00:09:58.328 --> 00:09:59.454
You took a while.

00:10:00.079 --> 00:10:02.415
Yeah, I did a loop
around the neighborhood.

00:10:02.624 --> 00:10:03.708
Go back to sleep.

00:10:06.461 --> 00:10:08.588
"Yongmu Gym"?

00:10:12.050 --> 00:10:14.969
Don't put it in the laundry inside out.

00:10:15.887 --> 00:10:17.889
Okay, just go to bed already.

00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:29.901
Are you a foreigner?

00:10:29.984 --> 00:10:30.902
Watch out!

00:10:33.404 --> 00:10:35.073
Who sent you here? Tell me.

00:10:36.991 --> 00:10:39.035
"A new day is coming"?

00:10:52.924 --> 00:10:54.259
MAMMOSEU MART

00:10:54.342 --> 00:10:56.594
Min-seo, cut it out.

00:10:56.803 --> 00:11:00.056
I'm the only one
among my friends without it.

00:11:00.139 --> 00:11:03.351
I'll study really hard.
Just get me this, please?

00:11:04.227 --> 00:11:06.229
Please, Mom.

00:11:06.312 --> 00:11:08.147
Wake up.

00:11:08.231 --> 00:11:11.276
What middle-school student
wears sneakers that cost 500,000 won?

00:11:11.526 --> 00:11:15.071
Don't you see your mom and dad
working to the bone here?

00:11:15.154 --> 00:11:15.989
Take this.

00:11:16.447 --> 00:11:18.783
- But Mom.
- Gosh.

00:11:18.866 --> 00:11:20.994
You don't need to call me that so loudly.

00:11:21.703 --> 00:11:24.831
The whole town knows I'm your mom already.

00:11:25.123 --> 00:11:26.666
Are you really not getting them for me?

00:11:26.749 --> 00:11:29.794
No, you can save the money
and get a pair for yourself.

00:11:32.547 --> 00:11:35.091
- You're so mean.
- Whatever.

00:11:37.218 --> 00:11:38.511
Was I adopted?

00:11:46.436 --> 00:11:48.896
You think adopting is easy?
That costs money, you know?

00:11:49.689 --> 00:11:50.690
Goodness.

00:11:56.112 --> 00:11:57.947
- Hello.
- Hey, Myeong-o.

00:11:58.031 --> 00:11:59.198
What's with Min-seo?

00:12:06.914 --> 00:12:08.124
What's with the butane gas?

00:12:08.374 --> 00:12:09.792
Oh, these.

00:12:09.876 --> 00:12:11.878
You know the butane gas
that exploded in the ATM?

00:12:11.961 --> 00:12:13.796
- They're recalling them all.
- I see.

00:12:14.339 --> 00:12:16.382
Your first day at work
is coming soon, isn't it?

00:12:16.466 --> 00:12:17.342
Yes.

00:12:17.717 --> 00:12:21.804
Your mom is over the moon
because you work for a big company now.

00:12:21.888 --> 00:12:24.098
She said she'd host a party
for the Women's Association.

00:12:24.265 --> 00:12:25.475
My gosh, Mom.

00:12:25.808 --> 00:12:26.893
Why shouldn't she?

00:12:26.976 --> 00:12:30.813
If Min-seo went to Hanguk University
and got a good job like you,

00:12:30.897 --> 00:12:33.566
I'd host a party for the entire town
with a whole pig and a cow.

00:12:33.649 --> 00:12:38.071
I'd be practically
dancing around the streets.

00:12:38.154 --> 00:12:39.781
But look at her.

00:12:40.156 --> 00:12:43.326
She just asked if she was adopted
just because I wouldn't buy her sneakers.

00:12:43.409 --> 00:12:44.952
Min-seo is smart.

00:12:45.119 --> 00:12:48.456
Jeong-hwan said she was a quick learner
with great comprehension skills.

00:12:48.539 --> 00:12:49.791
He never lies.

00:12:49.999 --> 00:12:52.085
- Really?
- Of course.

00:12:53.753 --> 00:12:57.507
Anyway, thanks for introducing me
to such a great tutor.

00:12:57.924 --> 00:12:59.050
It's nothing.

00:12:59.384 --> 00:13:01.094
- I'll get going now.
- Okay.

00:13:01.177 --> 00:13:03.262
- Have a good day.
- You, too.

00:13:05.807 --> 00:13:06.849
Of course.

00:13:07.517 --> 00:13:09.477
It's impossible for her to be stupid
if she takes after me.

00:13:20.446 --> 00:13:21.656
This is better than I expected.

00:13:23.157 --> 00:13:24.951
You'll get the basics down soon.

00:13:25.701 --> 00:13:28.663
Why didn't you try hard in school
when you're so smart?

00:13:32.125 --> 00:13:33.918
I'm complimenting you. Why the long face?

00:13:34.460 --> 00:13:38.131
Sullivan credits his parents
for all his success.

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:41.175
His birth parents abandoned him,

00:13:41.634 --> 00:13:43.886
but his adoptive parents
gave him everything.

00:13:44.720 --> 00:13:47.014
He said he got a second chance at life,
thanks to being adopted,

00:13:47.473 --> 00:13:49.642
which eventually led him to success.

00:13:51.352 --> 00:13:54.272
Did you save up your own money
to get your car?

00:13:54.605 --> 00:13:56.732
No, my parents helped me.

00:13:56.816 --> 00:14:00.778
My mom wants me to save up
and buy my own sneakers.

00:14:03.865 --> 00:14:05.074
By the way,

00:14:07.493 --> 00:14:09.579
do you have a girlfriend?

00:14:09.996 --> 00:14:10.913
No.

00:14:14.292 --> 00:14:16.711
That's why studying
is my biggest interest nowadays.

00:14:16.794 --> 00:14:19.589
I don't know why I haven't tried harder
with such a smart brain.

00:14:21.507 --> 00:14:22.925
Should I move on to the next question?

00:14:24.510 --> 00:14:26.804
Sure, here's your pen.

00:14:39.150 --> 00:14:40.026
Honey.

00:14:41.235 --> 00:14:42.236
You got changed?

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:43.988
Where are you going now?

00:14:44.071 --> 00:14:45.948
The youth association president
wants to see me.

00:14:46.782 --> 00:14:47.867
I'll be right back.

00:14:47.992 --> 00:14:49.118
What youth association president?

00:14:50.119 --> 00:14:53.498
It's the hardware store owner.

00:14:54.665 --> 00:14:56.209
He looks too old to be a youth, though.

00:14:57.084 --> 00:15:00.421
Anyway, the owner of the grocery store
is the head of the Women's Association,

00:15:00.505 --> 00:15:03.132
and the owner of the laundry place is
the head of the neighborhood association.

00:15:03.216 --> 00:15:05.927
What an organized neighborhood, right?

00:15:06.719 --> 00:15:07.595
Anyway, see you.

00:15:10.765 --> 00:15:14.894
It's dangerous out today,
so stay home with Do-yeon, okay?

00:15:16.395 --> 00:15:17.480
What's dangerous?

00:15:20.441 --> 00:15:22.652
The micro dusts.

00:15:22.735 --> 00:15:26.155
The pollution level is crazy today.

00:15:26.948 --> 00:15:28.449
It's life-threatening.

00:15:29.158 --> 00:15:29.992
See you.

00:15:35.790 --> 00:15:39.669
Why are you going out, then?

00:15:39.752 --> 00:15:41.921
Why?

00:15:42.338 --> 00:15:43.256
Here.

00:15:45.383 --> 00:15:48.970
If this is an assassination attempt,
you should've chosen the right poison.

00:15:50.471 --> 00:15:54.141
I'm very immune.
Not just any poison gets to me.

00:15:55.518 --> 00:15:59.188
Do they train you
for assassination attempts at JDD?

00:16:01.399 --> 00:16:04.569
There's no such training. Come on, man.

00:16:05.111 --> 00:16:08.364
You're the one who mentioned
all that about being immune.

00:16:08.447 --> 00:16:10.283
I was just trying to be nice.

00:16:10.366 --> 00:16:14.745
So why are you suddenly being nice?
Of course I'll get suspicious.

00:16:14.829 --> 00:16:18.124
And all Korean dads are immune.

00:16:18.207 --> 00:16:20.334
From eating all the food
their kids drop on the floor.

00:16:22.837 --> 00:16:24.130
Whatever.

00:16:24.213 --> 00:16:25.923
I served in the HID unit

00:16:26.424 --> 00:16:28.843
until I had to transfer
to the Maintenance Battalion.

00:16:29.302 --> 00:16:30.344
Okay, whatever.

00:16:31.470 --> 00:16:32.763
Let me just ask you one thing.

00:16:33.681 --> 00:16:35.474
How old are you, Mr. Hardware?

00:16:37.143 --> 00:16:38.060
Me?

00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:42.523
I was a freshman in 1998.

00:16:42.607 --> 00:16:45.526
What? So was I.
Born in the year of the sheep?

00:16:47.194 --> 00:16:48.654
No way!

00:16:48.863 --> 00:16:51.157
I didn't expect to meet
someone my age in my neighborhood.

00:16:52.325 --> 00:16:53.909
Hey, buddy. Nice to meet you.

00:16:55.453 --> 00:16:57.955
You're changing the topic.
You're younger than me, aren't you?

00:16:58.039 --> 00:17:01.292
Who changed the topic? You did, not me.

00:17:01.375 --> 00:17:03.377
Whatever.

00:17:04.879 --> 00:17:06.547
Tell me more about the JDD unit.

00:17:11.844 --> 00:17:15.681
You know what acid the army can't handle?

00:17:17.308 --> 00:17:19.644
An acid the army can't handle?

00:17:21.562 --> 00:17:23.272
Nitric acid? No.

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:25.441
No, sulfuric acid.

00:17:26.734 --> 00:17:30.613
Amino acid!

00:17:30.696 --> 00:17:32.698
Army-no acid! You know?

00:17:32.782 --> 00:17:36.118
You can't make your whole personality
about serving without even knowing this.

00:17:36.661 --> 00:17:38.579
Are you sure you're from the HID unit?

00:17:39.914 --> 00:17:41.624
Where's the gun? I have to shoot you.

00:17:42.541 --> 00:17:44.543
Are you kidding me?

00:17:44.627 --> 00:17:45.628
Hey, honey.

00:17:45.711 --> 00:17:46.921
Where are you, Daddy?

00:17:47.004 --> 00:17:48.547
Hey, my cutie.

00:17:48.673 --> 00:17:50.925
I'm just out for a bit.
I'll be right back.

00:17:52.760 --> 00:17:53.761
Okay.

00:17:55.096 --> 00:18:00.768
Come to the street pub at the intersection
after dinner tonight.

00:18:01.018 --> 00:18:02.728
I'm grabbing a drink with the guys.

00:18:02.978 --> 00:18:05.898
You should get to know your neighbors.

00:18:05.981 --> 00:18:07.274
Aren't I right, buddy?

00:18:08.693 --> 00:18:10.236
Let me ask you a favor.

00:18:10.319 --> 00:18:14.448
Let's not talk about the no comment thing
around others, all right?

00:18:14.949 --> 00:18:16.158
Sure, friend.

00:18:24.083 --> 00:18:25.626
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

00:18:25.710 --> 00:18:28.421
He's one of us now, okay?

00:18:28.504 --> 00:18:30.589
- Sure.
- Yes, pleased to meet you.

00:18:30.673 --> 00:18:31.924
Likewise.

00:18:32.007 --> 00:18:33.759
Feels like you're one of us already.

00:18:34.719 --> 00:18:39.390
I like you now a lot better than
when you were acting up at the hospital.

00:18:39.473 --> 00:18:42.643
- What's your name? Choi...
- Choi Kang.

00:18:42.768 --> 00:18:45.271
You look so gentle,
yet your name means "the strongest."

00:18:45.354 --> 00:18:47.398
What a strong boy.

00:18:47.982 --> 00:18:50.359
I don't know about anything else,
but my name never loses.

00:18:51.193 --> 00:18:54.238
I have a name women quite like, too.

00:18:54.321 --> 00:18:57.074
You know "Kim Su-il's diamond," right?

00:18:57.158 --> 00:19:00.619
I used to seduce women
by promising a fist-sized diamond.

00:19:00.703 --> 00:19:04.498
Who'd understand
the "Kim Su-il's diamond" reference now?

00:19:04.582 --> 00:19:07.251
Do you even know how much diamonds cost?

00:19:07.334 --> 00:19:09.378
You know how much a fist-sized one is?

00:19:09.462 --> 00:19:11.922
You have no idea, do you?

00:19:12.006 --> 00:19:13.716
- Why don't I take that fist
- My gosh.

00:19:13.799 --> 00:19:15.885
and break all your teeth?

00:19:15.968 --> 00:19:18.512
Sorry that things have been chaotic
since you moved.

00:19:18.596 --> 00:19:20.181
We rarely have incidents like these.

00:19:20.598 --> 00:19:23.058
Things were great around here
when the housing prices skyrocketed

00:19:23.142 --> 00:19:24.685
after the specialized zone announcement.

00:19:25.269 --> 00:19:28.606
Kang, how old are you?
Around Byeong-nam's age?

00:19:28.689 --> 00:19:31.192
Yeah, we were freshmen in college
in the same year.

00:19:31.275 --> 00:19:32.276
We're the same age.

00:19:32.359 --> 00:19:33.819
Then born in the year of the monkey?

00:19:33.903 --> 00:19:36.405
So you're also 12 years younger than me.

00:19:37.031 --> 00:19:39.033
I was born in the year of the sheep.

00:19:40.409 --> 00:19:45.331
Little Byeong-nam here may look rough,
but he can be quite cute.

00:19:45.414 --> 00:19:47.708
Stop it. All my friends
were born in the year of the sheep.

00:19:47.792 --> 00:19:49.543
And we're friends
if we were freshmen in the same year.

00:19:49.627 --> 00:19:52.421
Sure, kiddo. I'll let it slide.

00:19:52.505 --> 00:19:54.507
Have a drink, little bro.

00:19:54.590 --> 00:19:56.425
He was born in the year of the monkey.

00:19:57.551 --> 00:19:59.595
- Whatever.
- Here you go.

00:19:59.678 --> 00:20:01.764
Hey, we haven't gotten together
since that night.

00:20:01.847 --> 00:20:03.265
- Right.
- Ji-hun.

00:20:03.349 --> 00:20:05.476
You were also here
on the night of the accident.

00:20:05.559 --> 00:20:10.356
Yeah, I had to stay here until sunrise
to clean up at the pub.

00:20:10.439 --> 00:20:12.691
- You must've been scared, too.
- I was scared out of my mind.

00:20:12.775 --> 00:20:14.193
- Enjoy.
- Okay.

00:20:14.735 --> 00:20:16.111
Goodness.

00:20:16.195 --> 00:20:17.988
So Byeong-nam has an early birthday?

00:20:18.072 --> 00:20:18.948
Give me a moment.

00:20:25.454 --> 00:20:26.413
Excuse me.

00:20:26.956 --> 00:20:29.792
Did you happen to see
the driver of the other car,

00:20:29.875 --> 00:20:31.877
not the truck?

00:20:32.169 --> 00:20:35.339
I don't know
about the driver of the other car.

00:20:36.006 --> 00:20:39.426
But a tow truck came
when the firefighters put out the fire.

00:20:40.052 --> 00:20:42.471
And the tow truck just took that car.

00:20:42.555 --> 00:20:45.599
Do you remember
the color of the tow truck or its company?

00:20:46.392 --> 00:20:47.893
No, I don't.

00:20:47.977 --> 00:20:49.353
Anything else?

00:20:49.436 --> 00:20:52.147
You must've seen something
since you stayed here all night.

00:20:55.651 --> 00:20:56.485
Oh, right.

00:20:56.986 --> 00:21:02.157
And a 2.5t truck came
and cleaned up the site.

00:21:02.241 --> 00:21:04.451
Judging by their light packs,
they seemed like the standby squad.

00:21:05.578 --> 00:21:08.080
A 2.5t truck? You mean a military truck?

00:21:08.914 --> 00:21:11.917
Yeah, I know it because
I drove one as a military driver.

00:21:12.835 --> 00:21:14.461
They looked like
the Logistic Support Group.

00:21:14.753 --> 00:21:17.590
Back in the day, they specialized
in flood and forest fire recovery,

00:21:17.673 --> 00:21:21.677
so I was surprised to see them
clean up after a car accident that night.

00:21:23.429 --> 00:21:24.263
Thanks.

00:21:25.347 --> 00:21:26.181
All right, then.

00:21:34.273 --> 00:21:36.609
There was military involvement
in both cases?

00:21:38.152 --> 00:21:39.445
Why did they take the other car?

00:22:19.777 --> 00:22:21.070
What?

00:22:21.612 --> 00:22:23.155
- Damn it.
- Get your tools!

00:22:23.238 --> 00:22:24.406
Hurry! Go!

00:23:06.073 --> 00:23:09.535
A tow truck came
when the firefighters put out the fire.

00:23:09.618 --> 00:23:11.996
And the tow truck just took that car.

00:23:12.371 --> 00:23:14.790
Apparently, he took the damaged car
and drove toward Hanbal Mountain.

00:23:15.207 --> 00:23:18.127
There's nothing
on the other car or the driver.

00:23:18.377 --> 00:23:20.504
No idea whether they're alive or dead.

00:23:20.671 --> 00:23:21.922
But the other car is more at fault.

00:23:32.433 --> 00:23:34.393
What? Why is this open?

00:23:37.021 --> 00:23:38.063
What?

00:23:38.647 --> 00:23:39.732
Is that a frog?

00:23:41.400 --> 00:23:42.234
Hey, sort it out.

00:24:34.578 --> 00:24:35.621
Darn it!

00:24:36.038 --> 00:24:38.082
I can't do anything
when it won't even turn on.

00:24:38.665 --> 00:24:41.335
Do what?

00:24:45.005 --> 00:24:47.007
Hey, it's the perfect time
for instant noodles.

00:24:47.883 --> 00:24:49.009
Instant noodles sound good.

00:24:49.093 --> 00:24:50.511
Yeah, let's have some before we continue.

00:24:55.599 --> 00:24:57.476
- Is it still not turning on?
- No.

00:24:57.976 --> 00:24:59.353
Damn it.

00:25:04.316 --> 00:25:06.985
- How many?
- Three packs?

00:25:07.152 --> 00:25:09.738
Three? Just for you?

00:25:17.621 --> 00:25:19.414
VEOTIGO INSURANCE

00:25:19.498 --> 00:25:20.457
Yes.

00:25:23.210 --> 00:25:24.044
Yes.

00:25:26.713 --> 00:25:28.132
We're not done investigating yet.

00:25:28.340 --> 00:25:31.677
Why are you still investigating?
The autopsy and funeral ended days ago!

00:25:31.760 --> 00:25:33.554
We're doing our best.

00:25:33.637 --> 00:25:35.722
Damn it, this is so frustrating.

00:25:35.806 --> 00:25:37.057
BENEFICIARY DESIGNATION FORM
My sister still has to live

00:25:37.141 --> 00:25:39.476
even if her husband died!

00:25:39.935 --> 00:25:42.437
The woman with the baby who just left.

00:25:42.521 --> 00:25:44.398
Her husband died
in the intersection accident.

00:25:44.481 --> 00:25:46.733
She only ever buys products
that are on sale.

00:25:47.276 --> 00:25:49.528
Her kid is too young for her to work.

00:25:49.945 --> 00:25:52.322
Of course, I understand.

00:25:53.532 --> 00:25:55.576
THE CONFIRMED BENEFICIARIES ARE
HIS WIFE, LEE SEO-HUI, AND HIS 2 CHILDREN

00:25:55.659 --> 00:25:56.493
Yes, sir.

00:26:00.038 --> 00:26:02.166
Kang, did you finish your report?

00:26:04.626 --> 00:26:07.796
Soldiers came late that night
to clean up after the accident.

00:26:07.880 --> 00:26:10.257
The street pub server
across the street saw it.

00:26:10.340 --> 00:26:12.009
Soldiers? Man!

00:26:12.968 --> 00:26:15.596
It'll get complicated
with soldiers in the equation.

00:26:16.513 --> 00:26:17.931
Let's just close the case here.

00:26:19.141 --> 00:26:22.728
I'll file an emergency request
for the life insurance payout.

00:26:22.978 --> 00:26:24.438
They'll get the fund once it's approved.

00:26:24.521 --> 00:26:27.774
No, there are some bad guys
who are eyeing that money.

00:26:27.858 --> 00:26:30.777
So not yet. Just wait a bit.
Just a bit longer.

00:26:31.695 --> 00:26:34.406
You were begging me
to speed things up the other day.

00:27:00.182 --> 00:27:01.225
Hello?

00:27:06.605 --> 00:27:08.565
- Is anyone home?
- We work hard.

00:27:08.649 --> 00:27:11.652
So why can't you repay us?

00:27:12.319 --> 00:27:14.571
If you borrowed money,
you have to repay it.

00:27:14.655 --> 00:27:16.406
Huh? Don't you?

00:27:16.490 --> 00:27:18.408
Hey, look around and see
if she has any money.

00:27:18.492 --> 00:27:19.618
- Yes, sir.
- Go.

00:27:32.631 --> 00:27:34.883
- Stay here.
- Where's the money?

00:27:34.967 --> 00:27:38.762
Hey, don't break anything.
Just look carefully, okay?

00:27:39.554 --> 00:27:40.847
Yes, carefully.

00:27:41.390 --> 00:27:43.558
Come on.

00:27:43.892 --> 00:27:47.396
We don't want the whole town to know
she can't repay her debt.

00:27:48.689 --> 00:27:51.650
Use the yellow crayon.
It's a sunflower, man.

00:27:51.733 --> 00:27:53.235
With black in the middle.

00:27:53.318 --> 00:27:54.653
- Are you colorblind?
- Hello, ma'am.

00:27:56.738 --> 00:27:58.365
I'm Choi Kang

00:27:59.157 --> 00:28:00.325
of the SIU unit.

00:28:00.409 --> 00:28:01.868
I see.

00:28:01.952 --> 00:28:04.579
I had to come to tell you something.

00:28:05.664 --> 00:28:07.165
I'll just sit here.

00:28:08.834 --> 00:28:10.460
Listen to me carefully, okay?

00:28:12.004 --> 00:28:13.505
Once the inheritance process starts,

00:28:13.588 --> 00:28:16.758
the beneficiaries take on
the deceased’s debts as well.

00:28:16.842 --> 00:28:18.385
So, file a renunciation of inheritance
with the court.

00:28:18.468 --> 00:28:21.471
But every beneficiary
must file the renunciation.

00:28:22.389 --> 00:28:26.226
Now, would the renunciation prevent you
from taking the life insurance payout?

00:28:26.310 --> 00:28:27.144
No.

00:28:27.644 --> 00:28:30.105
Even if you renunciate inheritance,

00:28:30.188 --> 00:28:34.401
you can get the life insurance payout,
as it's the beneficiary's own asset.

00:28:34.901 --> 00:28:38.613
Even if debt collectors come to you,
demanding that you pay them back,

00:28:39.114 --> 00:28:40.574
you can just ignore them.

00:28:46.038 --> 00:28:48.123
What's that punk even saying?

00:28:48.707 --> 00:28:50.375
Is he from an insurance company?

00:28:50.459 --> 00:28:51.626
I think so, sir.

00:28:53.045 --> 00:28:54.921
Remember what I told you

00:28:55.005 --> 00:28:57.174
and do exactly that, okay?

00:28:58.508 --> 00:29:01.136
Yes, thank you.

00:29:02.763 --> 00:29:04.014
You must be So-yul.

00:29:04.264 --> 00:29:06.016
You're so cute.

00:29:07.184 --> 00:29:08.352
All right.

00:29:11.646 --> 00:29:13.231
Eat something good with your mom.

00:29:13.982 --> 00:29:18.362
And get some ice cream,
but don't share it with the baby, okay?

00:29:19.029 --> 00:29:20.989
Yes, thank you.

00:29:21.073 --> 00:29:24.159
What a damn beautiful sight.

00:29:24.242 --> 00:29:25.619
Go and have some food.

00:29:26.244 --> 00:29:27.454
Sure.

00:29:30.874 --> 00:29:33.543
- I'll talk to them. Don't worry and go.
- Okay.

00:29:34.127 --> 00:29:36.380
Get me some ice cream, too!

00:29:36.463 --> 00:29:38.799
The twisty bar kind, okay?

00:29:40.717 --> 00:29:41.843
Hey, insurance.

00:29:43.387 --> 00:29:44.513
Come here.

00:29:44.596 --> 00:29:47.682
Why are you interrupting our business?

00:29:48.016 --> 00:29:50.018
Come here, you punk.

00:29:50.644 --> 00:29:51.853
Just don't kill them.

00:29:55.315 --> 00:29:56.691
Don't kill them.

00:30:04.658 --> 00:30:06.743
Hey, you want to die?

00:30:07.285 --> 00:30:09.079
How dare you ignore the boss--

00:30:36.356 --> 00:30:37.441
You done writing it?

00:30:38.024 --> 00:30:38.900
Yes, sir.

00:30:40.569 --> 00:30:45.031
Table, 3,000,000 won.
Chairs, 2,000,000 won.

00:30:45.449 --> 00:30:46.867
What kind of chair costs that much?

00:30:46.950 --> 00:30:49.995
We have to get a whole new set to match.

00:30:50.912 --> 00:30:52.205
The chairs look fine.

00:30:54.666 --> 00:30:55.709
Yes, sir.

00:30:56.418 --> 00:30:58.837
Next, 1,000,000 won for the coffee table.

00:30:59.129 --> 00:31:00.297
That's a rip-off, isn't it?

00:31:00.380 --> 00:31:02.799
Yes, it is. It's too cheap, isn't it?

00:31:03.592 --> 00:31:04.426
No, sir.

00:31:06.595 --> 00:31:08.722
You put your cigarette on the table?

00:31:10.891 --> 00:31:13.268
Add 500,000 won for cleaning.

00:31:13.518 --> 00:31:15.395
What? For cleaning?

00:31:15.479 --> 00:31:17.814
That's how much it costs
to clean a home when moving in.

00:31:17.898 --> 00:31:18.732
Write it down.

00:31:19.983 --> 00:31:20.817
Yes, sir.

00:31:22.360 --> 00:31:26.448
When you're done, write the date,
your name, and phone number, and sign it.

00:31:27.741 --> 00:31:28.658
Give it to me.

00:31:29.451 --> 00:31:30.285
Yes, sir.

00:31:34.706 --> 00:31:36.124
SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT

00:31:36.208 --> 00:31:38.418
It's 6,500,000 won in total, right?

00:31:39.503 --> 00:31:40.462
Yes.

00:31:40.545 --> 00:31:41.838
Darn it, my pants.

00:31:43.048 --> 00:31:45.634
Hey, add 7,000 won for dry cleaning.

00:31:45.842 --> 00:31:46.760
Dry cleaning?

00:31:51.848 --> 00:31:53.683
No, it's not what you think!

00:31:53.767 --> 00:31:55.852
I'll just give you the 7,000 won now.

00:31:56.436 --> 00:31:57.270
Hold on.

00:31:59.731 --> 00:32:01.608
Here you go.

00:32:05.487 --> 00:32:06.530
Listen, buddy.

00:32:07.197 --> 00:32:09.407
I don't bully people into giving me money,
like you guys do,

00:32:09.491 --> 00:32:11.785
so I'll only take the maximum legal rate
of 20 percent.

00:32:12.536 --> 00:32:13.662
Pay me on time, okay?

00:32:14.037 --> 00:32:14.871
Yes, sir.

00:32:24.589 --> 00:32:25.924
- You're getting a call.
- Yes, sir.

00:32:26.841 --> 00:32:28.802
That's my number, okay?

00:32:28.885 --> 00:32:30.637
- Okay.
- Don't ignore it.

00:32:31.054 --> 00:32:32.430
I'll text you my bank account number.

00:32:33.765 --> 00:32:34.849
Yes, have a good day, sir.

00:32:36.309 --> 00:32:38.144
I'll clean it up here. Have a good day.

00:32:39.062 --> 00:32:40.480
SPECIAL MARTIAL ARTS YONGMU GYM

00:32:40.564 --> 00:32:42.566
Have a great day, ma'am.

00:32:43.024 --> 00:32:44.568
- Salute!
- Salute!

00:32:44.651 --> 00:32:46.903
All right, see you tomorrow!

00:32:47.904 --> 00:32:49.281
Do-yeon, show me your power!

00:32:49.364 --> 00:32:51.074
Go!

00:32:53.368 --> 00:32:54.536
Do-yeon!

00:32:55.078 --> 00:32:56.413
Dad!

00:32:56.871 --> 00:32:59.082
- Hello, sir!
- Hi.

00:33:02.168 --> 00:33:04.629
You look great as always!

00:33:04.713 --> 00:33:06.423
- Hello.
- Hi.

00:33:06.506 --> 00:33:08.383
Do-yeon, let's say goodbye and go.

00:33:08.842 --> 00:33:09.801
Salute!

00:33:09.884 --> 00:33:11.136
Salute!

00:33:11.219 --> 00:33:12.596
See you tomorrow, Do-yeon.

00:33:12.679 --> 00:33:13.555
Let's go.

00:33:15.599 --> 00:33:16.600
Oh, sorry.

00:33:17.058 --> 00:33:19.477
I think it's going to take some time.

00:33:19.561 --> 00:33:20.562
Sure.

00:33:20.645 --> 00:33:24.274
They even changed the login information
in that brief moment that night.

00:33:24.983 --> 00:33:26.276
They're total pros.

00:33:26.359 --> 00:33:29.321
Okay, I'm sure you can sort it out.
I trust you.

00:33:29.404 --> 00:33:31.573
It's just that
there's a lot that I don't know.

00:33:31.656 --> 00:33:33.074
I'm learning as I go.

00:33:33.533 --> 00:33:35.535
- Okay.
- Goodbye.

00:33:36.369 --> 00:33:37.329
Okay, then.

00:33:38.246 --> 00:33:40.457
- Bye, Do-yeon.
- Goodbye!

00:33:46.963 --> 00:33:48.423
Hello, sir.

00:33:48.506 --> 00:33:49.883
Hey, Do-yeon.

00:33:49.966 --> 00:33:51.301
- Have you been good?
- Yes.

00:33:52.927 --> 00:33:53.928
So, all is good?

00:33:54.262 --> 00:33:56.222
Dad, what does that mean?

00:33:56.890 --> 00:33:58.892
He's just asking how I'm doing.

00:34:01.311 --> 00:34:03.021
All is well with you, too, little bro?

00:34:03.438 --> 00:34:05.398
Of course, buddy.

00:34:08.860 --> 00:34:10.278
Let's say goodbye to him and go.

00:34:10.362 --> 00:34:12.113
Goodbye, sir.

00:34:12.197 --> 00:34:13.365
Get home safely.

00:34:13.448 --> 00:34:14.741
- Okay.
- Bye.

00:34:42.560 --> 00:34:45.313
MAGNIFYING MEDIA
I was just about to talk about that.

00:34:45.397 --> 00:34:49.192
We'll establish a strong security system
to prevent this from recurring

00:34:49.275 --> 00:34:52.445
and install smart security cameras

00:34:52.529 --> 00:34:54.698
- that can predict potential danger
- Does she take speech classes or what?

00:34:54.781 --> 00:34:56.324
- and send alerts.
- She's all talk.

00:34:56.408 --> 00:34:58.827
On top of that, I'll make sure
to hold people legally accountable...

00:34:58.910 --> 00:35:00.203
VIDEO UPLOADED

00:35:00.286 --> 00:35:02.288
...for the unfortunate incidents
that have recently happened...

00:35:02.872 --> 00:35:03.873
Man.

00:35:09.379 --> 00:35:10.463
Let's go home.

00:35:30.191 --> 00:35:34.654
UNKNOWN: A NEW DAY IS COMING

00:35:40.785 --> 00:35:44.038
MAMMOSEU MART

00:35:53.214 --> 00:35:55.967
KIYUN BUS TERMINAL

00:35:57.427 --> 00:35:59.429
- Hello.
- Good morning.

00:35:59.763 --> 00:36:01.765
- The bus will leave in three minutes.
- Yes, sir.

00:36:49.687 --> 00:36:52.482
#FIRST DAY TO WORK, #SUITED UP, #EXCITED,
#CAN'T WAIT FOR MY FIRST PAYCHECK

00:36:52.565 --> 00:36:53.566
Crazy guy.

00:36:55.193 --> 00:36:56.861
What a busy life.

00:37:47.537 --> 00:37:53.543
THIRD EXPLOSION
ON AUG 22, 2025 AT 5:50 A.M.

00:37:56.045 --> 00:37:59.132
We have a lot of deliveries this morning.
I made a list on the counter.

00:37:59.215 --> 00:38:00.884
- Okay.
- I'll drop Min-seo off and be right over.

00:38:00.967 --> 00:38:02.802
- Prepare the packages while I'm gone.
- Got it.

00:38:02.886 --> 00:38:04.971
- Have a good day at school.
- Okay.

00:38:06.055 --> 00:38:09.183
She's so cranky this morning.
She didn't even eat breakfast.

00:38:09.642 --> 00:38:11.269
All because I won't buy her new sneakers.

00:38:14.397 --> 00:38:15.732
Do you smell smoke?

00:38:17.609 --> 00:38:19.068
Is someone burning something?

00:38:20.153 --> 00:38:22.322
Anyway, drive safe.
Don't let your temper make you speed.

00:38:22.405 --> 00:38:25.408
- What temper?
- What? I didn't say anything. See you.

00:38:43.468 --> 00:38:45.553
If your grades improve
in the next midterm period,

00:38:46.512 --> 00:38:48.723
I'll get you those crazy sneakers.

00:38:50.016 --> 00:38:52.352
Really? You promise?

00:38:53.353 --> 00:38:54.604
Really, Mom?

00:38:54.771 --> 00:38:57.315
Of course. Have I ever lied?

00:38:57.565 --> 00:38:58.691
Never mind if you don't want it.

00:38:59.525 --> 00:39:02.236
Hey! You're making the van shake.

00:39:02.904 --> 00:39:04.864
Gosh, are you that happy?

00:39:04.948 --> 00:39:06.199
Yeah, totally.

00:39:06.282 --> 00:39:08.534
Mom, say that again
so that I can record it.

00:39:08.785 --> 00:39:09.953
What?

00:39:10.036 --> 00:39:13.581
Come on. I'll listen to it
whenever I don't want to study.

00:39:13.831 --> 00:39:15.833
My goodness.

00:39:17.418 --> 00:39:20.505
Min-seo, it's me, your mom.

00:39:20.964 --> 00:39:23.508
If your grades improve
in the next midterm season,

00:39:24.384 --> 00:39:27.679
I'll buy those crazy 500,000-won sneakers
for you.

00:39:28.179 --> 00:39:30.390
But you get nothing
if your grades drop, okay?

00:39:30.890 --> 00:39:31.933
Promise.

00:39:32.517 --> 00:39:33.851
Promise.

00:39:42.193 --> 00:39:43.486
Was there an accident or something?

00:39:52.370 --> 00:39:54.330
Mom, I see firetrucks there.

00:39:54.664 --> 00:39:56.207
That's the bus terminal, right?

00:39:58.751 --> 00:40:00.753
Did the smoke smell come from there?

00:40:11.055 --> 00:40:15.059
What happened?
Why have they blocked the road?

00:40:27.113 --> 00:40:28.990
EMERGENCY MEDICAL CENTER

00:40:32.577 --> 00:40:34.037
- How's the patient?
- He's unconscious.

00:40:34.120 --> 00:40:34.954
Unconscious?

00:40:35.663 --> 00:40:36.706
Careful.

00:40:43.671 --> 00:40:45.798
UNIDENTIFIED MALE IN HIS 20S

00:40:48.301 --> 00:40:50.011
ARMY18 8285

00:40:55.224 --> 00:40:56.434
MAMMOSEU MART

00:40:56.517 --> 00:40:59.312
All the Changri-dong leaders are here.

00:40:59.395 --> 00:41:01.105
- Heading to work?
- Yes.

00:41:03.024 --> 00:41:04.734
Are you having a serious discussion?

00:41:04.817 --> 00:41:07.570
Don't even get us started.
A bus exploded. It's crazy.

00:41:07.820 --> 00:41:08.821
What?

00:41:09.030 --> 00:41:11.824
A bus exploded at the bus garage.

00:41:12.408 --> 00:41:13.576
Did anyone get hurt?

00:41:13.659 --> 00:41:15.286
No idea. We're just as in the dark.

00:41:15.369 --> 00:41:17.705
Nobody won't tell us anything,
and it's not even on the news.

00:41:18.539 --> 00:41:19.791
Oh, right.

00:41:19.874 --> 00:41:22.710
You must know,
since you work for an insurance company.

00:41:22.794 --> 00:41:26.506
Who are the first responders
when such an accident happens?

00:41:27.548 --> 00:41:31.135
If it's a big one,
the police, ambulance, and firefighters.

00:41:31.219 --> 00:41:32.762
Insurance company people also come.

00:41:33.096 --> 00:41:34.931
See? That's normal.

00:41:35.014 --> 00:41:36.974
What were soldiers doing there?

00:41:37.141 --> 00:41:38.101
Soldiers?

00:41:38.184 --> 00:41:40.895
I got a glimpse of the site
when I drove Min-seo to school

00:41:40.978 --> 00:41:42.438
and saw military trucks.

00:41:44.982 --> 00:41:46.067
Hello.

00:41:46.275 --> 00:41:48.236
Even the Joint Chiefs
and the commander's lead car were there.

00:41:48.319 --> 00:41:50.029
- Joint Chiefs and the commander?
- Yeah.

00:41:52.573 --> 00:41:54.492
What do you mean?

00:41:54.784 --> 00:41:58.037
There's Myeong-o's friend.
Min-seo's tutor.

00:41:58.621 --> 00:42:01.249
Wait, I'll call him. I have his number.

00:42:01.332 --> 00:42:03.584
Don't cry and stay put, okay?

00:42:04.377 --> 00:42:05.795
- Ms. Lee?
- Yes.

00:42:05.878 --> 00:42:06.921
What did she say?

00:42:07.004 --> 00:42:10.925
Myeong-o left for work,
but she can't reach him.

00:42:11.134 --> 00:42:13.177
He left early this morning
to catch the first bus.

00:42:13.261 --> 00:42:15.596
I'm sure he's fine.

00:42:19.267 --> 00:42:22.478
Hello, this is Min-seo's mom.

00:42:22.562 --> 00:42:25.314
Have you talked to Myeong-o today,
by any chance?

00:42:28.609 --> 00:42:31.279
There's been an accident,
and your son was...

00:42:33.281 --> 00:42:34.365
Ma'am!

00:42:34.907 --> 00:42:36.742
- Call the ambulance!
- Let's take my car.

00:42:36.826 --> 00:42:37.869
- I got her!
- Okay!

00:42:37.952 --> 00:42:39.203
Please help.

00:42:39.287 --> 00:42:41.038
- Here we go.
- Pull yourself together!

00:42:45.126 --> 00:42:46.085
So,

00:42:47.044 --> 00:42:50.423
soldiers cleaned up the intersection
after the explosion,

00:42:51.007 --> 00:42:54.719
and firefighters cleaned up
the ATM explosion in combat boots.

00:42:55.303 --> 00:42:57.305
Now, when the bus terminal blew up,

00:42:58.055 --> 00:43:00.558
the Joint Chiefs
and the commander's lead car came?

00:43:01.434 --> 00:43:02.560
Yes.

00:43:03.019 --> 00:43:04.103
And all three were explosions.

00:43:04.562 --> 00:43:07.565
You said you saw ashy smoke
in the car crash at the intersection, too.

00:43:07.648 --> 00:43:09.859
Su-il remembers it very clearly.

00:43:10.943 --> 00:43:12.904
The same thing happened
in the ATM explosion.

00:43:13.196 --> 00:43:14.864
Chun-bae saw the explosion this morning.

00:43:15.364 --> 00:43:16.449
More ashy smoke.

00:43:21.287 --> 00:43:22.205
A C-4.

00:43:24.415 --> 00:43:25.499
It must've been a C-4.

00:43:26.000 --> 00:43:28.085
Of course, it could be a modified bomb.

00:43:29.879 --> 00:43:30.922
Ours again?

00:43:31.756 --> 00:43:32.715
You sure?

00:43:33.090 --> 00:43:35.092
This is driving me nuts.

00:43:37.678 --> 00:43:38.638
I know you're in there.

00:43:39.597 --> 00:43:40.598
Let's talk later.

00:43:46.145 --> 00:43:48.981
Why the hell aren't you
picking up your damn phone?

00:43:49.065 --> 00:43:50.566
Did you call?

00:43:50.650 --> 00:43:52.985
Oh, you called a lot.

00:43:53.653 --> 00:43:55.780
It's better to see you in person, anyway.

00:43:55.863 --> 00:43:56.739
You kidding me?

00:43:57.823 --> 00:44:00.826
Two people died in a bus explosion.

00:44:00.910 --> 00:44:03.079
And one is barely hanging on in the ICU.

00:44:04.121 --> 00:44:05.414
Lower your voice, will you?

00:44:05.790 --> 00:44:07.333
You think this is your living room?

00:44:10.753 --> 00:44:14.674
It just wouldn't be good
to have people outside hear us.

00:44:15.341 --> 00:44:16.342
Have a seat.

00:44:21.889 --> 00:44:23.599
What sneaky stuff
have you done behind my back

00:44:23.683 --> 00:44:25.518
that we have something blowing off
every day?

00:44:25.893 --> 00:44:28.938
And why is it my Kiyun-si, of all places?

00:44:29.355 --> 00:44:32.817
Everyone's already making a big deal
about Sullivan pulling out

00:44:32.900 --> 00:44:36.279
and making the plan
for the specialized zone become nothing!

00:44:36.362 --> 00:44:37.947
You should be helping, not doing this!

00:44:38.030 --> 00:44:39.740
You think I know what's going on?

00:44:39.991 --> 00:44:42.368
This is a headache for me, too, okay?

00:44:42.451 --> 00:44:44.412
I have to clean up the mess,
shush the prosecution and the police,

00:44:44.495 --> 00:44:45.997
and stop the press!

00:44:46.080 --> 00:44:48.207
I haven't even had time
for a sauna lately.

00:44:48.291 --> 00:44:49.875
You know I've got a bad shoulder, right?

00:44:49.959 --> 00:44:52.003
From getting tortured back in the day?

00:44:53.337 --> 00:44:55.464
You're awfully good at keeping secrets

00:44:56.841 --> 00:44:58.384
for someone who's shit at everything.

00:44:59.093 --> 00:45:01.595
Why won't anyone tell me anything?

00:45:01.804 --> 00:45:05.516
I'm asking you what's been exploding!

00:45:05.599 --> 00:45:08.936
You're to become
the nation's leader one day!

00:45:09.020 --> 00:45:11.272
Don't say stuff like "shit."

00:45:12.982 --> 00:45:16.652
You're already on the same boat as I am.

00:45:16.944 --> 00:45:19.780
I also went all-in on making Kiyun-si
a specialized tourism zone.

00:45:19.864 --> 00:45:24.201
That's why I'm busy cleaning the mess
before everything falls apart.

00:45:24.285 --> 00:45:26.245
Just tell me what's going on!

00:45:26.329 --> 00:45:29.957
How am I supposed to know?
I'm still figuring it out too!

00:45:34.837 --> 00:45:38.215
Minister Kim, are you sure
you don't know anything?

00:45:38.799 --> 00:45:41.177
It's my responsibility
to clean up this mess, isn't it?

00:45:41.260 --> 00:45:45.639
So leave it to me
and cut the bullshit, okay?

00:45:52.271 --> 00:45:55.900
I'll kill you if you pull anything stupid
behind my back.

00:46:04.909 --> 00:46:08.079
I ought to put a bullet
in that rude bitch.

00:46:08.871 --> 00:46:10.164
Damn it.

00:46:48.994 --> 00:46:53.124
OUR DEEPEST CONDOLENCES

00:46:53.207 --> 00:46:56.127
MAY THE DECEASED REST IN PEACE

00:46:56.210 --> 00:46:59.463
KIM MYEONG-O

00:47:11.934 --> 00:47:14.019
They say people live up to their names.

00:47:14.520 --> 00:47:16.897
You really are the strongest
when it comes to being nosy.

00:47:17.731 --> 00:47:20.151
I can't believe you're going to a funeral
for someone you've never even met.

00:47:20.484 --> 00:47:24.447
All the neighborhood leaders
knew him well.

00:47:24.738 --> 00:47:28.659
My friend's friend is also my friend.
How could I turn a blind eye?

00:47:29.368 --> 00:47:31.245
He was the only son of a single mother,

00:47:31.537 --> 00:47:32.997
graduated from Hanguk University,

00:47:33.080 --> 00:47:35.583
and spent three years working part-time
while looking for a job.

00:47:36.000 --> 00:47:37.793
Then he finally got
a big corporate job recently.

00:47:39.837 --> 00:47:43.132
It was his first day at work,
and he died on the way.

00:47:43.883 --> 00:47:46.218
You make it sound
like he was your best friend.

00:47:46.969 --> 00:47:49.221
I wasn't going to go this far,

00:47:51.640 --> 00:47:54.810
but the bestie
of my bestie's bestie is also my bestie.

00:47:55.144 --> 00:47:57.563
And you're my bestie for life,

00:47:57.646 --> 00:47:59.398
- so you should--
- Enough.

00:48:00.274 --> 00:48:03.068
Give a good amount of consolation money,
but not too much.

00:48:04.361 --> 00:48:05.279
Yes, ma'am.

00:48:07.239 --> 00:48:09.825
Don't go out.
Stay home with Do-yeon, okay?

00:48:09.909 --> 00:48:12.161
If you need anything,
just let me get it for you, like always.

00:48:12.244 --> 00:48:13.329
Okay, just go.

00:48:14.538 --> 00:48:17.541
FUNERAL HALL 1
Did you say you need her permission?

00:48:17.833 --> 00:48:20.753
- Of course, I do.
- Really?

00:48:25.382 --> 00:48:30.888
Man, I used to feel so bad for Su-il
for having such a controlling wife,

00:48:31.138 --> 00:48:34.141
but here you are, just like him.

00:48:34.350 --> 00:48:36.685
Controlling? No, I'm just playing along.

00:48:36.977 --> 00:48:38.395
You need her permission
to go to a funeral.

00:48:38.479 --> 00:48:40.397
How's that playing along?
You're totally whipped.

00:48:41.273 --> 00:48:44.818
You don't seem the type,
but you're surprisingly sharp.

00:48:45.903 --> 00:48:48.489
What are these reporters
doing here anyway?

00:48:48.572 --> 00:48:50.157
To interview the bereaved?

00:48:50.324 --> 00:48:52.576
They're not asking anyone anything.

00:48:53.077 --> 00:48:54.703
I guess a high-ranking official is here.

00:48:55.704 --> 00:48:56.622
Let's go.

00:49:09.552 --> 00:49:10.553
- She's here!
- She's here!

00:49:19.895 --> 00:49:21.981
The only thing improving
is my acting these days.

00:49:23.148 --> 00:49:24.441
All right, let's go.

00:49:27.945 --> 00:49:30.114
- What's going on in Kiyun-si?
- Please tell us!

00:49:30.197 --> 00:49:31.865
- What do you have to say?
- What happened?

00:49:31.949 --> 00:49:33.492
- Please look this way!
- What's going on?

00:49:33.576 --> 00:49:35.494
- Ma'am!
- What'll happen now?

00:49:36.453 --> 00:49:39.623
Please let me pay my respects
before taking questions.

00:49:39.707 --> 00:49:41.792
- What's the scale of the damage?
- How many casualties?

00:49:41.875 --> 00:49:43.961
- Please tell us!
- What happens now?

00:49:44.044 --> 00:49:46.338
- Please say something.
- Just one thing!

00:50:23.375 --> 00:50:26.420
You must stay strong, ma'am.

00:50:27.713 --> 00:50:31.008
I can't live on.

00:50:33.135 --> 00:50:34.970
My son...

00:50:38.682 --> 00:50:42.853
I can't live without my son.

00:50:42.936 --> 00:50:46.023
My Myeong-o...

00:50:46.106 --> 00:50:50.069
Please bring him back.

00:50:52.279 --> 00:50:55.074
Myeong-o, take me with you!

00:50:55.157 --> 00:50:57.826
Take me with you!

00:50:57.910 --> 00:50:58.952
Ma'am.

00:51:01.538 --> 00:51:05.793
I promise to investigate
the cause of Myeong-o's death.

00:51:07.294 --> 00:51:12.049
Thank you so much. My Myeong-o...

00:51:18.847 --> 00:51:20.307
Why are you here? What about the store?

00:51:20.391 --> 00:51:23.644
I closed it for a bit
and came with Chun-bae.

00:51:23.727 --> 00:51:26.021
I said we should work in shifts.
You couldn't even wait that long?

00:51:27.106 --> 00:51:29.108
Don't be so cruel.

00:51:29.191 --> 00:51:32.569
Closing your business for a few hours
for your dead neighbor isn't--

00:51:34.905 --> 00:51:36.240
You think it's because of the money?

00:51:37.199 --> 00:51:39.451
We're the only functioning grocery store
in the neighborhood.

00:51:39.535 --> 00:51:42.496
I'm worried about those
who urgently need anything from the store.

00:51:46.333 --> 00:51:47.459
Eat quickly and go.

00:51:47.543 --> 00:51:49.420
Yeah, I don't have an appetite, anyway.

00:51:50.421 --> 00:51:52.423
What a woman.

00:51:52.923 --> 00:51:56.093
Why do you always use me as an excuse?
I came here alone.

00:51:56.385 --> 00:51:58.387
Are you a bad friend, or just clueless?

00:51:58.470 --> 00:51:59.471
Just eat your food.

00:52:03.892 --> 00:52:06.478
FUNERAL HALL

00:52:17.906 --> 00:52:20.117
I think we're done for the day now.

00:52:20.200 --> 00:52:22.995
Come and eat some.
You haven't eaten all day.

00:52:24.037 --> 00:52:25.622
I'm fine.

00:52:30.335 --> 00:52:33.797
Ms. Lee needs you to stay strong
more than anyone right now.

00:52:33.881 --> 00:52:36.133
You can't faint with her.

00:52:36.216 --> 00:52:38.719
Come and have something to eat.

00:52:59.907 --> 00:53:02.701
- Hey, Yong-hui.
- Hello.

00:53:02.785 --> 00:53:04.620
Sorry, I'm late.
I had to close up the gym.

00:53:06.038 --> 00:53:07.581
Go and greet Myeong-o.

00:53:07.831 --> 00:53:08.916
Okay.

00:53:10.459 --> 00:53:11.668
Myeong-o...

00:53:13.086 --> 00:53:14.338
My goodness...

00:53:19.635 --> 00:53:20.844
You haven't eaten, have you?

00:53:20.928 --> 00:53:22.638
No, I ate. Stay seated.

00:53:27.893 --> 00:53:30.521
This is Min-seo's tutor.

00:53:30.729 --> 00:53:32.940
He's Myeong-o's friend.
Myeong-o introduced him to me.

00:53:33.690 --> 00:53:36.527
And this is the manager
of Special Martial Arts Yongmu Gym.

00:53:36.610 --> 00:53:38.195
He used to be
a close neighbor of Myeong-o.

00:53:38.529 --> 00:53:40.781
I see. I'm Park Jeong-hwan.

00:53:40.864 --> 00:53:42.741
I'm Lee Yong-hui.

00:53:43.283 --> 00:53:44.660
You must be heartbroken.

00:53:45.911 --> 00:53:46.745
Yes.

00:53:52.084 --> 00:53:53.001
You know,

00:53:55.087 --> 00:53:56.880
I still can't believe it.

00:53:59.258 --> 00:54:00.467
None of us can.

00:54:01.593 --> 00:54:05.430
Ms. Lee says she feels like
Myeong-o will come in any minute,

00:54:05.848 --> 00:54:09.309
still in his suit, saying, "I'm home!"

00:54:10.602 --> 00:54:15.274
I wish I could've seen him in his suit.

00:54:24.908 --> 00:54:25.909
Here.

00:54:28.203 --> 00:54:30.122
Oh, it's Myeong-o.

00:54:33.333 --> 00:54:34.918
- My gosh.
- Look at him.

00:54:35.002 --> 00:54:39.673
Our Myeong-o suited up nicely for work.
He even wore a tie and everything.

00:54:40.257 --> 00:54:41.925
I know, gosh.

00:54:42.009 --> 00:54:43.594
Oh, would you like something?

00:54:44.386 --> 00:54:46.096
I just need to use the bathroom.

00:54:46.179 --> 00:54:47.097
Okay.

00:54:56.773 --> 00:54:58.400
There's a stuffed bunny.
A gift for someone?

00:54:58.483 --> 00:54:59.902
This one's a video.

00:55:00.986 --> 00:55:03.405
It must be so nice to start the day
with a surprise gift like that.

00:55:16.710 --> 00:55:17.878
What's wrong, Yong-hui?

00:55:18.462 --> 00:55:20.213
I need to go.

00:55:23.884 --> 00:55:25.135
What's with him?

00:55:35.062 --> 00:55:36.104
Byeong-nam!

00:55:36.521 --> 00:55:37.356
What?

00:55:38.148 --> 00:55:40.192
- You know the bunny?
- What about them?

00:55:40.275 --> 00:55:43.737
The bus was on the bunny!

00:55:43.820 --> 00:55:45.322
What are you talking about?

00:55:45.405 --> 00:55:47.449
Wake up! How could a bus be on a...

00:55:50.786 --> 00:55:52.496
- A bunny?
- Yes!

00:55:52.913 --> 00:55:56.041
There was a stuffed bunny

00:55:56.375 --> 00:55:59.002
sitting on the bus!

00:55:59.086 --> 00:56:02.130
- How do you know?
- Myeong-o took a video of it.

00:56:02.214 --> 00:56:05.467
- Can I see it? Let's see.
- Yes!

00:56:08.845 --> 00:56:11.014
THIS IS A PRIVATE ACCOUNT

00:56:11.098 --> 00:56:11.932
It's private.

00:56:12.015 --> 00:56:13.642
What? Where is it?

00:56:13.725 --> 00:56:16.186
I don't follow Myeong-o
on social media, so...

00:56:16.269 --> 00:56:19.147
- Come on, how can we see it?
- How did you see it?

00:56:19.231 --> 00:56:21.066
At the funeral hall.

00:56:23.485 --> 00:56:25.070
On Myeong-o's friend's phone.

00:56:39.292 --> 00:56:40.460
Excuse me.

00:56:42.129 --> 00:56:44.881
Could we see Myeong-o's post from earlier?

00:56:55.726 --> 00:56:58.270
- This thing, right?
- Right.

00:56:58.353 --> 00:57:01.732
The stuffed bunnies at the recycling area
also had a sweet and oily scent.

00:57:02.024 --> 00:57:03.525
What do you mean?

00:57:04.317 --> 00:57:05.444
The C-4.

00:57:05.652 --> 00:57:06.737
What?

00:57:07.195 --> 00:57:08.196
A bomb?

00:57:08.989 --> 00:57:10.198
What do you mean?

00:57:14.244 --> 00:57:17.122
You left after looking at these photos.
What's going on?

00:57:17.205 --> 00:57:18.915
Oh, I mean...

00:57:18.999 --> 00:57:21.084
Just tell me everything.

00:57:21.793 --> 00:57:23.420
This is my friend we're talking about.

00:57:29.301 --> 00:57:32.429
There seems to have been
a bomb on the bus.

00:57:40.062 --> 00:57:41.772
Who would've put it there?

00:57:44.524 --> 00:57:46.359
Who would've done that?

00:57:46.651 --> 00:57:49.696
It's dangerous, so we'll sort it--

00:57:49.780 --> 00:57:50.906
No.

00:57:52.157 --> 00:57:53.241
I...

00:57:55.285 --> 00:57:56.995
I want to find

00:57:58.955 --> 00:57:59.998
the bastard

00:58:01.083 --> 00:58:02.459
behind all this.

00:58:31.655 --> 00:58:34.783
SPECIAL MARTIAL ARTS YONGMU GYM

00:58:37.160 --> 00:58:39.371
Good, but tilt it up a bit.

00:58:41.248 --> 00:58:42.666
Thanks for working so hard in the heat.

00:58:42.958 --> 00:58:44.835
- Please be thorough.
- Yes, of course.

00:58:44.918 --> 00:58:45.877
Okay.

00:58:52.509 --> 00:58:55.512
I keep my promises.

00:58:55.595 --> 00:58:58.723
We're installing smart AI security cameras

00:58:58.807 --> 00:59:03.770
to ensure safety
for the Changri-dong residents.

00:59:05.647 --> 00:59:07.149
I know you must be so worried.

00:59:07.566 --> 00:59:08.608
Of course.

00:59:08.692 --> 00:59:12.028
How can there be so many accidents
in Changri-dong nonstop?

00:59:15.574 --> 00:59:19.661
I'll make sure accidents like this
never happen again.

00:59:23.290 --> 00:59:25.292
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

00:59:25.375 --> 00:59:28.295
These are getting set up
in front of schools too, right?

00:59:28.378 --> 00:59:31.464
What a joke. Fussing over cameras
after everything's already happened.

00:59:31.715 --> 00:59:33.008
Honey, she might hear you.

00:59:33.091 --> 00:59:34.426
I don't care if she does.

00:59:34.759 --> 00:59:36.678
Actually, I hope she hears me.

00:59:38.054 --> 00:59:41.057
They're going to monitor us with those.

00:59:41.600 --> 00:59:43.143
Hey, bad news for you.

00:59:43.727 --> 00:59:47.439
Even Choi Kang, the man of no comments,
can't escape all those cameras, can you?

00:59:48.773 --> 00:59:51.610
You want to bet
on whether I can escape them or not?

00:59:54.905 --> 00:59:56.531
I'll bet 500 won that I can't.

00:59:56.948 --> 00:59:58.366
You bet that I can, little bro.

01:00:00.911 --> 01:00:02.412
Stay right here, okay?

01:00:02.495 --> 01:00:05.248
I'll bring a gun right over
and actually shoot you.

01:00:05.540 --> 01:00:07.209
You're too gullible.

01:00:07.459 --> 01:00:09.920
- What?
- It's so much fun to tease you.

01:00:11.296 --> 01:00:12.339
Stop it.

01:00:12.964 --> 01:00:14.007
I told you to stop.

01:00:14.966 --> 01:00:17.719
Hey, I'm telling you, cut it out.

01:00:17.802 --> 01:00:19.304
Stop. I'm getting my gun.

01:00:32.275 --> 01:00:35.111
Online security cameras. That's great.

01:00:35.946 --> 01:00:37.948
Why? You can't hide from those?

01:00:39.115 --> 01:00:41.952
That's not it. If that's online,

01:00:42.035 --> 01:00:44.412
the satellite computer guys
must be watching them, too.

01:00:44.663 --> 01:00:46.206
But what would you know?

01:00:46.957 --> 01:00:48.959
So what? What are you going to do?

01:00:49.876 --> 01:00:51.294
Play along, of course.

01:00:57.008 --> 01:00:58.468
Are you crazy?

01:00:58.551 --> 01:01:00.470
I'm not crazy. They are.

01:01:07.227 --> 01:01:10.563
- One, two, three.
- Two, three.

01:01:12.399 --> 01:01:15.193
- Wait. One, two, three.
- Three.

01:01:15.277 --> 01:01:17.529
- Yeah, you jerks. Take this.
- Take this.

01:01:17.612 --> 01:01:19.489
- Take this.
- Take this.

01:01:19.572 --> 01:01:21.950
- Take this.
- You little rats.

01:01:45.098 --> 01:01:46.474
Take this, too.

01:01:47.100 --> 01:01:49.561
- Keep going.
- Take this. Come on.

01:01:49.644 --> 01:01:51.896
One, two, three, go!

01:02:35.815 --> 01:02:38.735
HEROES NEXT DOOR

01:02:38.818 --> 01:02:41.821
It seems to have something to do
with the explosions in Kiyun-si.

01:02:42.155 --> 01:02:43.114
THEY'RE LISTENING, SHUSH

01:02:43.198 --> 01:02:44.866
Why are you telling me all this?

01:02:45.533 --> 01:02:46.451
WHAT IF WE USE IT AGAINST THEM?

01:02:46.534 --> 01:02:49.120
I brought something from Unit 203.

01:02:49.204 --> 01:02:51.414
The computer signal disconnected
at the police station,

01:02:51.498 --> 01:02:52.999
so these guys will go there.

01:02:53.083 --> 01:02:54.959
What are you guys plotting?

01:02:55.043 --> 01:02:58.046
People in our neighborhood are dying.
We need to do something.

01:02:59.047 --> 01:03:00.423
A bomb threat in Kiyun-si?

01:03:00.507 --> 01:03:01.383
- Stay back.
- Let me through.

01:03:01.466 --> 01:03:02.926
Arrest them right now
and interrogate them.

01:03:03.009 --> 01:03:04.094
Who are you?

01:03:04.177 --> 01:03:05.470
How did you know about this place?

01:03:06.388 --> 01:03:08.390
Subtitle translation by Min-sun Kim